# These findings are intentional in this demo repo — VMs need public internet access for SSH.

# AWS: subnet assigns public IPs (needed for demo VM reachability)
AWS-0164

# AWS: security group allows unrestricted SSH ingress (demo VM must be reachable)
AWS-0107

# Azure: NSG allows unrestricted ingress / SSH from any IP (demo VM must be reachable)
AZU-0047
AZU-0050

# GCP: instance has a public IP (needed for demo VM reachability)
GCP-0031

# These findings are intentional in the containerised-app demo modules.

# AWS: ALB is internet-facing (the demo exposes a public HTTP endpoint)
AWS-0053

# AWS: ALB listener uses plain HTTP (demo has no TLS certificate; HTTPS would require ACM)
AWS-0054

# AWS: security group allows unrestricted egress (ECS tasks must reach ECR/internet to pull
# images; ALB must forward responses back to clients — open egress is standard for both)
AWS-0104

# These findings are intentional in the serverless demo modules.

# AWS: CloudWatch log group for Lambda is not KMS-encrypted (same accepted LOW as containerised-app)
AWS-0017

# Azure: Functions runtime storage account network rules default to Allow — Deny blocks the Terraform
# runner's data-plane access (creating containers/blobs from GitHub Actions). Not fixable without
# a private endpoint or VNet integration, both overkill for a demo module.
AZU-0012

# Azure: Functions runtime storage account does not have blob logging enabled (internal runtime
# store, not a user-facing data store — enabling logging adds cost and complexity for no demo value)
AZU-0057

# Azure: Functions runtime storage account uses LRS not GRS (demo module — no HA requirement)
AZU-0058

# Azure: Functions runtime storage account does not use customer-managed keys (demo module)
AZU-0060

# Azure: Functions runtime storage account does not have infrastructure double-encryption (demo module)
AZU-0061
